{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/37983-bringing-tiers-to-wraith","id":37983,"title":"Bringing Tiers to Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-27T13:32:42-08:00","id":37983,"title":"Bringing Tiers to Wraith","content":"(We may be needing a Wraith dedicated forum sooner than expected with all these threads).<br /> <br /> Wraith has always been two games stuck together, in a sense. On one hand, you have the ring of newly-dead wraiths struggling through their newfound existence and trying to deal with their Passions, Fetters, Shadows, and all the other unpleasantness that comes with an existence on the dark side of the Shroud. On the other, you have the Hierarchy-Renegade-Heretic conflict and all sorts of distinctly Stygian politics that essentially make Wraith less a part of the World of Darkness and more a wholly independent setting. Reconciling these things is somewhat tough, and you end up with two distinct scales of play.<br /> <br /> In the nWoD, there's the notion of Tier, which had its start in Hunter but has since expanded to be a general sort of thing. It defines the scope of a chronicle and the support base of the PCs; Tier 1 is a distinctly personal story, with the Ring and maybe a few friends against the world, Tier 2 is the PCs zooming out a bit (this corresponds nicely with being a Hierarchy recruit or in a Renegade cell, and focusing on the machinations in the underworld a bit more), and Tier 3 is when the PCs can really throw some weight around in their organizations (I see this as being Doosmlayers, but that's a tad limited).<br /> <br /> In essence, it lets you tell the troupe just what exactly you'll be dealing with, and resolves the confusion of things a bit. I fear I may be rambling now. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T14:27:18-08:00","id":38010,"title":"","content":"Similar to Scion (Hero/Demigod/God) in some ways, yes. Wraith really is two entirely different games mushed together. I personally prefer focusing on the Shadowlands and their interaction with the living. I'd really love to see Wraith20 (Wraith Revised?) split the settings a bit further apart. The Shadowlands being the primary setting and moving the Tempest/Labyrinth off to the realm of a sub-setting like the Umbral Realms in Werewolf, Deep Dreaming in Changeling or Deep Umbra in Mage. <br /> <br /> You <i>can</i> play a Werewolf or Mage game based almost entirely in the Umbra. It has a very different theme, feel and social dynamic than a traditional game, but it's viable. I'd enjoy seeing that in Wraith as well. If you push the Tempest (and Stygia) further back, the setting becomes a lot more approachable for new players. It's not so much about them becoming cogs in the machine of a dystopian empire, as that dystopian empire being a looming presence on the horizon, at the edge of their world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T23:50:50-08:00","id":38179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/37983-bringing-tiers-to-wraith#post37983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(We may be needing a Wraith dedicated forum sooner than expected with all these threads).</div> </div> </div> </div> I know right? But the answer guys keep saying not till it's closer to the Wr20 development date. Ah well. Come to think of it even though Mage 20 is in development, I don't see much activity on the Mage sub forum. I hope Satyros will check in soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T08:32:32-08:00","id":38746,"title":"","content":"Satyros has been checking in on the Facebook page. A lot. <br /> <br /> I agree with the suggestion of implementing advice for \u201clow-tier play\u201d for games where the Dark Kingdoms and their politics are minimized, and wraiths deal primarily with their personal quests for Transcendence. Thing is, I wouldn\u2019t divide it between Shadowlands and Underworld: travel between the two is easy enough that Stygia <i>ought to</i> exert plenty of influence over the Shadowlands; and the Dictum Mortuum wouldn\u2019t mean much if its enforcers were largely disconnected from the place where the violations take place. <br /> <br /> Instead, I\u2019d use <b>End of Empire</b> as the partition: prior to the coming of the Sixth Great Maelstrom, the default paradigm is political intrigue, and personal quests for Transcendence take place within that context. After the Ghost Storm has arrived, the Dark Kingdoms are no more, and many surviving wraiths find that they\u2019ve been pushed across the Shroud into the Skinlands. The lack of a unified Empire of Iron combined with easier interaction with the living is almost custom-made for stories about resolving unfinished business. <br /> <br /> Which is not to say that \u201cregional\u201d or even \u201cglobal\u201d tiers would be impossible in the post-Reckoning setting; indeed, \u201crebuilding the Stygian Empire\u201d sounds like a grand storyline to try. But it wouldn\u2019t be presented as the default premise: for the most part, gaming after <b>End of Empire</b> would be optimized for games that have a personal or local scope, just as pre-<b>End of Empire</b> games are optimized for political intrigue in a dark fantasy world substantially removed from the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}